members.statement_original:
Let $\gamma$ be a probability measure on $\mathbb R_+^L$ with mean $\mathbf1$. Consider $x\ge0$. There exists a closed half-space $\mathbb H_x$ of $\mathbb R^L$ and a measure $\mu_x$ supported on $\mathbb H_x$, such that
(i) the positive diagonal $\mathcal I_L^+\not\subseteq\mathbb H_x$;
(ii) $-\mathbf1\in\mathbb H_x$;
(iii) $x\mathbf1\in\partial\mathbb H_x=\mathbb H_x\cap\mathbb H_x^c$, where $\mathbb H_x^c$ is the closed complement of $\mathbb H_x$;
(iv) the measure $\mu_{\mathbb H_x^c}:=\gamma-\mu_x$ is supported on $\mathbb H_x^c$, and the barycenters of $\mu_x$ and $\mu_{\mathbb H_x^c}$ both lie on $\mathcal I^+$.
In this case, we call $\partial\mathbb H_x$ a separating hyperplane at $x$. Moreover, if (N) holds, there exists a unique measure $\mu_x$ satisfying the above conditions, in which case it also holds that $\mu_x=\gamma|_{\mathbb H_x}$ and $\mu_{\mathbb H_x^c}=\gamma|_{\mathbb H_x^c}$.
